.TH VERITAS 1 "2026" "veritas 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
veritas \- discover and run Veritas test suites, tests and benchmarks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veritas
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B veritas
is the command line interface of the Veritas unit, integration and black box
testing framework for GNU Guile.
.PP
It walks a project looking for test files, loads each file's entry point and
runs it.  By default the entry point is a no-argument function called
.BR spec ,
files are looked up under
.B ./test
and test modules are expected to be named
.BR "(veritas unit ...)" .
.PP
Every option is a thin syntactic sugar over a
.B VERITAS_*
environment variable.  The command line therefore produces exactly the same
configuration as setting the environment by hand, which keeps local runs,
CI pipelines and programmatic runs reproducible and in sync.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-scan\-dir " " DIR
Root directory scanned for tests
.RB ( VERITAS_SCAN_DIR ,
default
.BR ./ ).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-test\-top\-dir " " DIR
Directory holding the test hierarchy
.RB ( VERITAS_TEST_TOP_DIR ,
default
.BR test ).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test\-type " " TYPE
Test category and sub-directory to load
.RB ( VERITAS_TEST_TYPE ,
default
.BR unit ).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-entrypoint " " NAME
No-argument function called inside every test file
.RB ( VERITAS_ENTRYPOINT ,
default
.BR spec ).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-test\-module " " NAME
Top level module prefix of the tests
.RB ( VERITAS_TEST_MODULE ,
default
.BR veritas ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reporter " " NAME
Reporter to use
.RB ( VERITAS_REPORTER ,
default
.BR emoji-reporter ).
Other built-in choices include
.B monotone-reporter
and
.BR json-reporter .
.TP
.B \-\-only\-test " " SUBSTR
Only run tests whose name contains
.IR SUBSTR
.RB ( VERITAS_ONLY_TEST ).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-suite " " SUBSTR
Only run suites whose name contains
.IR SUBSTR
.RB ( VERITAS_ONLY_SUITE ).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shuffle
Shuffle the order of discovered files (default;
.BR VERITAS_SHUFFLE_FILES=true ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shuffle
Keep the discovered file order
.RB ( VERITAS_SHUFFLE_FILES=false ).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-benchmarks
Run benchmarks (default;
.BR VERITAS_RUN_BENCHMARKS=true ).
Benchmarks always run sequentially so that the profiler produces sound
measurements.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-benchmarks
Skip benchmarks
.RB ( VERITAS_RUN_BENCHMARKS=false ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help page and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VERITAS_ENTRYPOINT
Entry point function name.  Defaults to
.BR spec .
.TP
.B VERITAS_SCAN_DIR
Directory to scan for tests.  Defaults to
.BR ./ .
.TP
.B VERITAS_TEST_TYPE
Test type directory.  Defaults to
.BR unit .
.TP
.B VERITAS_TEST_TOP_DIR
Test hierarchy root.  Defaults to
.BR test .
.TP
.B VERITAS_TEST_MODULE
Module prefix of the test suites.  Defaults to
.BR veritas .
.TP
.B VERITAS_SHUFFLE_FILES
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
Defaults to
.BR true .
.TP
.B VERITAS_RUN_BENCHMARKS
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
Defaults to
.BR true .
.TP
.B VERITAS_ONLY_TEST
Optional substring filter on test names.
.TP
.B VERITAS_ONLY_SUITE
Optional substring filter on suite names.
.TP
.B VERITAS_REPORTER
Reporter symbol.  Defaults to
.BR emoji-reporter .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All selected tests and benchmarks finished successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A test failed, an option was invalid, or an error occurred while loading or
running the tests.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the unit tests with the project defaults:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run the integration suite, without benchmarks, keeping file order:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-t integration \-\-no\-benchmarks \-\-no\-shuffle
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use the plain reporter and only run suites mentioning
.BR auth :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-r monotone\-reporter \-\-only\-suite auth
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inside a Guix development shell:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
guix shell \-m manifest.scm \-\- ./bin/veritas \-h
.EE
.RE
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
The same runner is available from a Guile REPL.  Load the CLI module to
inspect or reuse its configuration:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
(use\-modules (veritas cli))
(show\-help)
(run\-cli '("--test\-type" "unit"))
.EE
.RE
.PP
To run with the current environment without parsing a command line, call the
runner directly:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
((@ (veritas runner) run\-tests))
.EE
.RE
